WEBVTT

00:01.511 --> 00:04.552
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.620 --> 00:07.862
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.930 --> 00:11.039
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.107 --> 00:14.115
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.182 --> 00:17.893
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.961 --> 00:21.003
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.070 --> 00:22.608
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.676 --> 00:23.980
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.048 --> 00:27.156
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:37.643 --> 00:39.714
Oh, Lois, I'm so glad
you were able

00:39.781 --> 00:41.119
to make it
to dinner tonight.

00:41.187 --> 00:42.857
Oh, me, too, Mom.

00:42.925 --> 00:44.061
We haven't seen
you in ages.

00:44.129 --> 00:45.299
Oh, there you are.

00:45.367 --> 00:47.204
Did you find
the new bathroom okay?

00:47.272 --> 00:48.809
Uh-huh.

00:48.877 --> 00:51.384
I'm so sorry about
your father keeping us.

00:51.451 --> 00:53.055
He's probably down
at the dock

00:53.124 --> 00:54.894
tinkering with that
darn yacht of his.

00:54.962 --> 00:56.300
Oh, that's okay, Mom.

00:56.367 --> 00:57.971
We'll just have to
entertain ourselves for...

00:58.039 --> 00:59.443
Hey, Babs, settle something
for us.

00:59.511 --> 01:01.950
I wanted to bring, um, an owl
on this trip,

01:02.018 --> 01:03.322
but Lois wouldn't let me.

01:03.389 --> 01:05.059
Could you have
accommodated an owl?

01:05.127 --> 01:07.099
Well, I suppose there's
some room in the owlery,

01:07.167 --> 01:08.938
but I can't be certain.

01:09.006 --> 01:10.643
I'll take that as a yes.

01:10.711 --> 01:12.349
You owe Dr. Hoo an apology.

01:12.416 --> 01:13.886
Hey, can we change
the channel?

01:13.954 --> 01:15.458
<i>I'm tired of watching
Old Ships.</i>

01:15.525 --> 01:18.100
Peter, that's not a TV,
it's a painting.

01:18.167 --> 01:19.604
Actually, Lois,
it is a TV.

01:19.673 --> 01:22.246
<i>It's the PBS show
Old Ships.</i>

01:22.314 --> 01:24.587
Good, I hate PBS.

01:24.654 --> 01:27.295
ANNOUNCER:
This PBS program is brought
to you by generous grants

01:27.363 --> 01:29.167
from the Arthur Vining Davis
Foundations

01:29.235 --> 01:31.709
and the John D. and Catherine T.
MacArthur Foundation

01:31.777 --> 01:32.911
in association with

01:32.980 --> 01:34.517
the Corporation
for Public Broadcasting,

01:34.585 --> 01:36.791
with additional funding
by Archer Midland Whiteman

01:36.858 --> 01:38.831
Colgate Palmolive,
Exxon Mobil,

01:38.899 --> 01:41.973
and a 20 I found in a blazer
I wore to a wedding last year.

01:42.041 --> 01:45.384
Tonight, on Ken Burns' nine-part
series on street signs:

01:45.452 --> 01:48.159
"Part Four: Yield."

01:48.227 --> 01:51.135
OLD MAN:
Before they had the sign,
people just run into each other.

01:51.203 --> 01:53.910
I don't know, maybe, maybe
you had to see the first three

01:53.978 --> 01:55.783
to get this,
but I-I am completely lost.

01:55.851 --> 01:57.119
Lois, you said
there would be

01:57.187 --> 01:58.491
other men my
own age here.

01:58.558 --> 02:00.197
But there aren't,
and I'm bored.

02:00.264 --> 02:02.202
Look, Peter, why don't you
just grab a book

02:02.270 --> 02:03.874
off the shelf and be quiet?

02:03.941 --> 02:05.111
No! Books are jerks.

02:05.179 --> 02:06.449
Stop acting like a brat.

02:06.518 --> 02:08.421
What about a picture book?

02:08.489 --> 02:11.096
Only if it has a mirror
at the end of it,

02:11.163 --> 02:13.003
and it says, "How about you?"

02:16.715 --> 02:18.619
Oh, wow,

02:18.687 --> 02:21.094
look at these old photos
of you and Dad.

02:21.162 --> 02:22.632
This must be
around the time

02:22.700 --> 02:24.505
you guys were
first dating, huh?

02:24.573 --> 02:25.775
Oh dear, yes.

02:25.842 --> 02:29.185
Ah, your father was
so handsome back then.

02:29.253 --> 02:31.594
I remember the day we met.

02:36.140 --> 02:40.655
<i>It was one of those lovely,
warm summer days by the shore.</i>

02:40.723 --> 02:43.529
<i>Perfect giant beach ball
weather.</i>

02:43.597 --> 02:46.572
Would you like another
John Barrymore and soda?

02:46.640 --> 02:48.177
Ah, yes.
Thank you, Clarence.

02:48.246 --> 02:49.583
How are things
in Terriblehood?

02:49.651 --> 02:50.618
Terrible, sir.

02:50.686 --> 02:51.588
Good, good.

02:52.659 --> 02:54.497
Ah! You dumb bitch!

02:54.564 --> 02:56.604
<i>My friend and I
held our breath,</i>

02:56.672 --> 02:59.145
<i>wondering which one of us
he was talking to.</i>

03:00.784 --> 03:02.622
<i>But the lucky one was me.</i>

03:02.690 --> 03:05.397
<i>And from there,
our romance blossomed.</i>

03:07.238 --> 03:09.075
Boy, you can
take a punch,

03:09.143 --> 03:11.315
but at the same time,
you cowered a little bit.

03:11.383 --> 03:12.853
Now, that's a woman.

03:12.922 --> 03:14.258
(giggles)

03:14.326 --> 03:16.264
I love you, Pussycup.

03:16.332 --> 03:18.037
I love you, too.

03:18.105 --> 03:19.540
Now, let's kiss

03:19.609 --> 03:21.614
while the camera pans
over to the drapes.

03:24.390 --> 03:27.097
Good stuff happening
over here.

03:27.166 --> 03:28.536
All implied.

03:28.604 --> 03:31.411
<i>It was the happiest time
of our lives.</i>

03:31.479 --> 03:33.584
<i>Unfortunately,
that was the year</i>

03:33.652 --> 03:35.892
<i>the great war with Alaska
broke out,</i>

03:35.959 --> 03:38.466
<i>and even Carter's lofty
connections</i>

03:38.534 --> 03:40.572
<i>couldn't save him
from the draft.</i>

03:40.640 --> 03:42.010
(explosion)

03:42.078 --> 03:44.819
<i>In one of the bloodiest battles
of the war,</i>

03:44.887 --> 03:46.958
<i>Carter nearly lost his life
in the battle</i>

03:47.026 --> 03:50.235
<i>with the infamous,
walrus-backed Nanookwaffe.</i>

03:51.575 --> 03:53.378
(roaring)

03:53.447 --> 03:55.385
<i>But through all of it,</i>

03:55.453 --> 03:57.357
<i>Carter never forgot
to write to me daily</i>

03:57.425 --> 04:00.934
<i>to send his love
along with a mix tape.</i>

04:01.002 --> 04:03.443
CARTER:
Babs, you want to spend
a mind-blowing afternoon?

04:03.510 --> 04:05.382
Get stoned
and listen to this song.

04:05.451 --> 04:10.265
WOMAN: ♪ Jeepers, creepers,
where'd you get those peepers? ♪

04:10.332 --> 04:14.076
<i>But after some months,
the letters stopped coming,</i>

04:14.144 --> 04:17.620
<i>and I was certain
he had perished.</i>

04:17.688 --> 04:21.633
<i>So I took up with a young dandy
named Rodginald.</i>

04:21.701 --> 04:23.906
<i>He would bring me
small chocolates</i>

04:23.974 --> 04:27.083
<i>and sit in my front parlor
and pitch woo at me,</i>

04:27.151 --> 04:30.359
<i>taking my hand gently and
singing from bended knee</i>

04:30.428 --> 04:32.466
<i>the popular songs of his youth.</i>

04:32.534 --> 04:33.769
♪ Marry me ♪

04:33.837 --> 04:38.585
♪ And I will buy you
chewing gum. ♪

04:38.653 --> 04:40.725
<i>With no other suitors
to speak of,</i>

04:40.792 --> 04:43.400
<i>I agreed that I would
marry him forthwith,</i>

04:43.468 --> 04:47.278
<i>even though my heart
still belonged to Carter.</i>

04:47.346 --> 04:49.519
(elegant music playing)

04:49.587 --> 04:54.032
<i>I believe Rodginald knew this,
and he even tried to strike me</i>

04:54.099 --> 04:56.173
<i>in the manner to which
I had become accustomed.</i>

04:56.241 --> 04:57.209
(hands slapping)

04:57.277 --> 04:58.680
<i>But it wasn't the same.</i>

04:58.748 --> 05:01.121
<i>And then a miracle happened.</i>

05:05.068 --> 05:06.271
Babs!

05:06.338 --> 05:08.209
Carter!

05:19.579 --> 05:20.782
Oh!

05:21.986 --> 05:24.292
Oh, Carter,
you're alive!

05:24.360 --> 05:25.831
I've missed you so.

05:25.898 --> 05:28.472
Babs, be my wife!

05:28.540 --> 05:31.582
Oh, yes,
Carter, yes!

05:31.650 --> 05:34.457
Hey, that's my gal!

05:34.525 --> 05:36.898
Dear, sir,
I respectfully urge you

05:36.965 --> 05:39.273
to prepare yourself
for one devil of a skirmish!

05:46.128 --> 05:48.333
Oh, I always
love hearing
that story, Mom.

05:48.401 --> 05:51.242
I got a story about a fat guy
who's starving and bored.

05:51.310 --> 05:52.814
Look, Peter, if
you're that hungry,

05:52.882 --> 05:54.686
go down to the dock
and find Daddy,

05:54.753 --> 05:55.923
and we'll get
dinner started.

05:55.991 --> 05:57.562
You're not gonna get
dinner started.

05:57.630 --> 06:00.237
She's gonna tell that sloppy
old Spanish maid to do it.

06:00.305 --> 06:02.176
And she will, but only
because she needs money

06:02.244 --> 06:03.547
to pay for medicine

06:03.615 --> 06:05.754
for her prematurely overweight
son Diabeto.

06:05.822 --> 06:08.196
Mama, may I
have cookie?

06:08.264 --> 06:10.837
No, Diabeto,
roll back to kitchen.

06:10.904 --> 06:13.043
Oh...!

06:15.953 --> 06:16.988
Mr. Pewterschmidt!

06:17.057 --> 06:19.797
Mr. Pewterschmidt,
dinner's ready!

06:22.140 --> 06:23.876
Damn it, he can't hear me.

06:34.878 --> 06:36.683
(Pewterschmidt laughing)

06:40.228 --> 06:41.832
Ah, that was excellent.

06:41.899 --> 06:43.839
When I clenched it, you
took your fingers away.

06:43.905 --> 06:45.577
You were right
to do that.

06:45.644 --> 06:46.646
Oh, my God!

06:46.714 --> 06:47.683
(gasps)

06:47.751 --> 06:48.687
Mr. Pewterschmidt,

06:48.755 --> 06:50.659
you're having an affair?! Ew!

06:50.727 --> 06:52.364
No, no, this is my sister.

06:52.432 --> 06:54.471
Ew!
No, no, no, I'm impotent.

06:54.538 --> 06:57.112
Ew!
I mean, she looked at me
while I did it to myself.

06:57.180 --> 06:58.114
Ew!

06:58.183 --> 06:59.118
I mean, she's a man.

06:59.186 --> 07:01.192
Ew!

07:01.260 --> 07:03.800
We need more Es and Ws
down here now!

07:03.867 --> 07:04.837
MAN:
We're trying!

07:04.905 --> 07:06.307
We're running
out of letters!

07:06.375 --> 07:08.481
Just turn the Ms upside down
and send them down here!

07:08.549 --> 07:09.985
You can't
just do that!

07:10.053 --> 07:11.356
There's a lot of
paperwork before
you can...

07:11.424 --> 07:12.794
I don't care!
I'll take the heat!

07:12.862 --> 07:14.098
Just turn them over
and send them down!

07:19.793 --> 07:21.899
Mr. Pewterschmidt,
you're having an affair?!

07:21.967 --> 07:23.938
Now, look, Griffin,
you better not breathe a word

07:24.006 --> 07:25.511
about what you saw here.

07:25.578 --> 07:27.081
But how can you be
having an affair?

07:27.149 --> 07:28.118
What about Babs?

07:28.186 --> 07:29.289
That's not your concern.

07:29.357 --> 07:30.826
You didn't see anything.

07:30.894 --> 07:32.666
Remember that
or I'll ruin you.

07:32.734 --> 07:33.835
Okay, okay, I promise.

07:33.903 --> 07:35.542
I'll be as quiet
as a church mouse.

07:35.609 --> 07:37.379
Hey, Billy, I was
gonna have a party

07:37.448 --> 07:38.851
at the rectory
this evening.

07:38.919 --> 07:42.228
Do you like sacramental wine
and mouse Russell Crowe movies?

07:42.296 --> 07:43.900
Oh, boy, do I!

07:43.968 --> 07:45.673
Hey, can my sister come?

07:45.740 --> 07:47.144
No! She'd ruin it!

07:50.354 --> 07:52.059
Now, remember,
you keep your mouth shut

07:52.126 --> 07:53.296
about what you saw.

07:53.364 --> 07:54.833
Yes, sir, Mr.
Pewterschmidt.

07:56.138 --> 07:58.946
Oh, there you are, boys.

07:59.014 --> 08:00.619
Sorry, sweetheart,
I lost track of time.

08:00.686 --> 08:01.955
Right, Peter?

08:02.023 --> 08:04.932
(forced laugh)

08:05.000 --> 08:07.138
I'm Peter.

08:07.207 --> 08:08.209
Well, let's
eat, huh?

08:08.277 --> 08:09.612
You must be
starving, Peter.

08:09.681 --> 08:11.118
What am I,
on trial here?!

08:11.185 --> 08:13.692
Uh, maybe you should just
eat something, Peter.

08:13.760 --> 08:15.330
Go on, put some food
in your mouth.

08:15.399 --> 08:16.801
Y-Y-Yes, sir, I sure will,

08:16.869 --> 08:19.008
Mr. Cooterschmidt...
Pewterschmidt! Oh, God!

08:21.216 --> 08:23.021
Peter, are you
feeling all right?

08:23.089 --> 08:24.325
Oh, he's fine.

08:24.392 --> 08:26.765
You know how hungry a man
gets after a day at sea.

08:26.833 --> 08:27.802
He eats with porpoise.

08:27.869 --> 08:28.839
Ha-ha! Oop!

08:28.907 --> 08:30.409
Peter, for God's sake,

08:30.477 --> 08:32.283
you're always
an embarrassment
at the table.

08:32.351 --> 08:34.288
You should've seen him
when we had dinner

08:34.357 --> 08:35.760
with Paul McCartney's
ex-wife.

08:35.828 --> 08:38.201
He kept playing footsie
with her under the table.

08:38.268 --> 08:41.076
(giggling)

08:42.281 --> 08:43.350
(loud thunk)

08:43.418 --> 08:44.754
Oh, my God,
I'm so sorry!

08:48.433 --> 08:49.937
Um, hey, guys?

08:50.005 --> 08:52.043
Uh, I-I got
a problem.

08:52.111 --> 08:54.451
Um, you know how
Lois has that dad?
Yeah.

08:54.519 --> 08:56.758
Well, we were there
the other night for dinner,

08:56.826 --> 08:58.831
and I caught him cheating
with some bimbo.

08:58.899 --> 09:00.403
Oh, my God!
You're kidding!

09:00.471 --> 09:02.174
Anyway, he told me
not to tell anybody,

09:02.242 --> 09:04.716
but I'm having a real hard time
not telling Lois.

09:04.784 --> 09:06.187
How could you not?

09:06.254 --> 09:08.863
Peter, once entered into,
marriage is a sacred bond;

09:08.931 --> 09:12.340
an alliance blessed by God
and hallowed by the community.

09:12.408 --> 09:14.246
That's why I'll never opt for
the matrimonial condition.

09:14.314 --> 09:15.984
It wouldn't be fair to
the historical framework

09:16.052 --> 09:17.354
of the institution.

09:17.423 --> 09:19.929
But for those who do,
and then turn their back

09:19.997 --> 09:22.270
on its long-standing
convictions? Shame!

09:22.338 --> 09:24.711
This is unwelcome news,
Peter. Very unwelcome.

09:24.779 --> 09:27.018
Yeah, I know, but I
don't know what to do.

09:27.086 --> 09:28.623
It's really hard
keeping my mouth shut.

09:28.690 --> 09:29.927
Actually, you know
something, Peter,

09:29.995 --> 09:31.866
this, this could be
an opportunity for you.

09:31.935 --> 09:34.106
What do you mean?
Well, Lois's dad
is loaded.

09:34.175 --> 09:36.280
Y-You could probably get him
to pay through the nose

09:36.347 --> 09:37.784
to keep your mouth shut.

09:37.852 --> 09:39.858
Yeah, you could really
milk this thing, Peter.

09:39.926 --> 09:41.663
Huh, I never thought of it
like that.

09:41.730 --> 09:42.967
Wait a minute.
You're not serious.

09:43.036 --> 09:44.272
That's totally unethical.

09:44.340 --> 09:45.676
Yeah, Brian, no one
cares what you think.

09:45.743 --> 09:46.947
Peter, you could
make him your slave!

09:47.014 --> 09:49.119
Oh, man. He'd hate
that even more

09:49.187 --> 09:50.591
than he hates sitcom
two-parters.

09:50.659 --> 09:52.128
Tootie, it's 8:29!

09:52.197 --> 09:54.604
Now either try that beer
or dump it down the sink! Wait!

09:54.671 --> 09:57.947
Oh! Now, I have to wait a whole
week to find out if she gave in

09:58.015 --> 09:59.351
to peer pressure
at that drinking party!

10:02.562 --> 10:05.303
(door shuts)

10:05.371 --> 10:07.744
Carter! Carter, wake up!

10:07.811 --> 10:09.883
(snorts)
It's o--
it's okay, Lois.

10:09.952 --> 10:11.154
Daddy's just taking
your temperature.

10:11.223 --> 10:12.626
Wh-What?

10:12.694 --> 10:13.729
Wh-What is it?

10:13.797 --> 10:15.501
I heard a noise
downstairs.

10:15.568 --> 10:17.675
(sighs) I'll go
have a look.

10:17.742 --> 10:18.812
It's probably
just the wine.

10:18.880 --> 10:19.882
The wind, dear.

10:19.950 --> 10:21.286
Is that how you say that?

10:21.354 --> 10:22.757
I've only seen
that word written.

10:26.837 --> 10:29.143
(water splashing)

10:31.819 --> 10:33.557
Hi, Mr. Pewterschmidt.

10:33.625 --> 10:35.998
Griffin! What the hell
are you doing in my house?!

10:36.065 --> 10:38.572
Well, I was getting ready
to watch a movie on your big TV,

10:38.639 --> 10:40.545
but first I thought I'd use
your hot bubbly toilet.

10:40.613 --> 10:41.815
That's not a toilet!

10:41.883 --> 10:43.353
Hey, when's it go
down, by the way?

10:43.421 --> 10:44.725
It's just doing a lot
of loop-de-loops.

10:44.793 --> 10:46.530
Get the hell out of there,
you son of a bitch!

10:46.599 --> 10:49.672
Oh, no, no. No, you don't get
to talk to me like that anymore.

10:49.740 --> 10:51.278
Not unless you want me to blab

10:51.347 --> 10:52.481
about what happened
on the yacht.

10:52.549 --> 10:55.057
What are you getting at,
Griffin?

10:55.124 --> 10:57.899
That's right, you're gonna start
doing a lot of stuff for me.

10:57.966 --> 10:58.868
Like what?

10:58.937 --> 10:59.971
Well, for starters,

11:00.039 --> 11:01.477
you got more than one limo?
Yeah.

11:01.545 --> 11:03.315
You and me are gonna
do a limo joust.

11:03.383 --> 11:05.188
What the hell is that?

11:07.261 --> 11:08.531
All right, you ready?

11:08.599 --> 11:09.835
I don't want to do this.

11:09.902 --> 11:11.708
Go!
(tires squealing)

11:11.776 --> 11:12.644
(tires squealing)

11:27.457 --> 11:30.399
PETER:
That went exactly
as I wanted it to go.

11:35.582 --> 11:37.086
All right here's
your Mike and Ikes

11:37.154 --> 11:38.558
with all the
Ikes taken out.

11:38.625 --> 11:40.564
I hope you were careful,
'cause I swear to God,

11:40.631 --> 11:43.004
if I find one Ike in there,
I'm going straight to Babs.

11:43.072 --> 11:44.175
It's fine,
I double-checked.

11:44.243 --> 11:46.281
Here's your Mikes.
What's next?

11:46.349 --> 11:47.819
Next, I want you
to fly to France

11:47.887 --> 11:49.524
and tell French people
that a good-looking,

11:49.593 --> 11:51.264
depressed guy
smoking a cigarette

11:51.332 --> 11:52.867
is not a movie.

11:52.935 --> 11:54.741
(clearing throat)

11:54.809 --> 11:56.279
(over loudspeakers):
People of France,

11:56.347 --> 11:58.586
a good-looking, depressed guy

11:58.654 --> 12:00.224
smoking a cigarette

12:00.292 --> 12:02.030
is not a movie,

12:02.098 --> 12:04.905
and your sirens sound like
gay guys having a threesome.

12:04.973 --> 12:08.952
(European-style siren blaring)

12:13.667 --> 12:15.605
All right, you got my
catch phrases for me?

12:15.673 --> 12:18.647
I just want you to know
this was a huge pain in the ass.

12:18.716 --> 12:20.720
"Peter's new catch phrases,
by Carter Pewterschmidt."

12:20.788 --> 12:22.426
Title's all business.
I like that.

12:22.494 --> 12:24.298
Also, I've been under
the weather lately,

12:24.366 --> 12:26.204
so it may not be
my best work.

12:26.273 --> 12:27.775
"Shape up
or show me your balls."

12:27.844 --> 12:28.813
That's good.

12:28.880 --> 12:29.982
Really?

12:30.051 --> 12:31.252
How about this one?

12:31.321 --> 12:32.658
"In your face,
Nancy Grace."

12:32.726 --> 12:33.828
Oh, I love it.

12:33.896 --> 12:35.900
Oh, man, there are a lot
of good ones here.

12:35.968 --> 12:38.876
"Fire alarm?
I am the fire alarm.

12:38.945 --> 12:40.683
"Find your own
beach house, Crabby.

12:40.751 --> 12:42.588
Put that in your
office and frame it."

12:42.655 --> 12:43.959
The last one's
kind of lame.

12:44.027 --> 12:46.132
Did you get down to the one
at the bottom there?

12:46.200 --> 12:47.670
Which one?

12:47.738 --> 12:49.910
"On your mark,
get set, terrible."
No, this one here.

12:49.978 --> 12:52.218
"If you've got a problem,
take it up with my butt.

12:52.286 --> 12:54.324
He's the only one
that gives a crap."

12:54.392 --> 12:55.930
Oh, my God, that's it.
Yeah.

12:55.998 --> 12:57.367
That-that's the one.
I thought you'd like...

12:57.435 --> 12:58.604
You are amaz...

12:58.672 --> 12:59.575
LOIS:
Peter, dinner.

12:59.642 --> 13:01.212
Take it up with my butt,

13:01.280 --> 13:03.185
'cause he's the only one
who gives a crap.

13:03.252 --> 13:05.928
LOIS:
Wow, what a great sentence.

13:09.406 --> 13:12.046
You know, Lois, I've
noticed Peter and Carter

13:12.113 --> 13:14.285
spending a lot of time
together lately.

13:14.354 --> 13:16.459
It's nice to see them
finally getting on.

13:16.527 --> 13:18.398
I know. Who would
have thought, huh?

13:18.467 --> 13:20.304
PETER:
Boy, I can't wait
to get this home.

13:20.373 --> 13:22.778
<i>You know, I keep not laughing
at The Big Bang Theory,</i>

13:22.846 --> 13:25.420
and I figure it's got
to be the television, you know?

13:25.488 --> 13:29.131
TV this size-- forget it, it'll
have me laughing till I got
snots falling out of my nose.

13:29.199 --> 13:31.439
Carter, where are you
taking our television?

13:31.506 --> 13:32.910
I'm giving it
to Peter.

13:32.977 --> 13:34.582
What?! Why?

13:34.651 --> 13:36.688
Yeah, why, Carter?
(sighs)

13:36.756 --> 13:38.762
(mechanically):
Because Peter is the best

13:38.829 --> 13:41.804
and he is awesome and he makes
better laser sounds than I do.

13:41.873 --> 13:43.041
(makes laser sounds)

13:43.108 --> 13:44.613
Damn right.
You hear that, Lois?

13:44.681 --> 13:46.319
And he's not just saying that

13:46.386 --> 13:48.224
'cause I covered for him
about his affair.

13:48.292 --> 13:49.494
What?

13:49.562 --> 13:52.639
Carter, is this true?

13:52.707 --> 13:56.015
Yes, it's true.

13:56.083 --> 13:58.589
Oh... Oh, dear!
(cup breaking)

13:58.658 --> 14:00.228
(sobbing)

14:04.007 --> 14:06.314
Well, on your mark,
get set, terrible.

14:06.382 --> 14:07.684
(laughing)

14:07.752 --> 14:09.991
No, no, but I-I understand
that this is bad.

14:15.648 --> 14:17.422
You stupid fat bastard!

14:17.487 --> 14:19.031
How could you tell her
I had an affair?!

14:19.200 --> 14:19.835
We had a deal!

14:19.877 --> 14:22.049
Look, I think you're blowing
this out of proportion, Carter.

14:22.117 --> 14:23.387
She's divorcing me!

14:23.455 --> 14:24.925
Well, I don't blame her.

14:24.992 --> 14:27.099
Daddy, how could you
do this to Mom?

14:27.166 --> 14:28.635
You two were
perfect together.

14:28.704 --> 14:30.542
It was such a
close marriage.

14:30.611 --> 14:32.414
You know, maybe the two
of you splitting up

14:32.482 --> 14:33.786
is a blessing in disguise.

14:33.854 --> 14:35.424
I mean, there are obviously
some problems

14:35.492 --> 14:36.996
in your relationship.

14:37.064 --> 14:39.537
Who knows, maybe some time apart
could be just what you need.

14:39.605 --> 14:41.576
Yeah, plus think of all
the fun stuff you can do

14:41.644 --> 14:42.913
as a single guy.

14:42.982 --> 14:44.418
Like-like going to loud,
awful bars

14:44.486 --> 14:46.390
and not being able to heart
the mediocre-looking chick

14:46.459 --> 14:47.561
next to you say
something stupid.

14:47.629 --> 14:48.899
It's going to be awesome.

14:48.967 --> 14:50.571
I don't know how to do
anything like that.

14:50.639 --> 14:51.975
It's easy.

14:52.043 --> 14:53.947
I'll help you meet some
women, Mr. Pewterschmidt.

14:54.016 --> 14:56.189
Come on, it's been
50 years since I've
been on a date.

14:56.256 --> 14:58.128
Well, how'd you get that chick
on the boat, then?

14:58.196 --> 14:59.700
You know how
in that movie

14:59.768 --> 15:01.772
Liam Neeson gets his daughter back?
Yeah.

15:01.839 --> 15:04.246
Well, that was one of the girls
their dad didn't get back.

15:12.205 --> 15:13.442
What kind of
joint is this?

15:13.509 --> 15:14.645
Where's the
cigarette girl?

15:14.713 --> 15:16.384
Yeah, they don't
have those anymore.

15:16.452 --> 15:18.055
Peter, I don't know
about this.

15:18.123 --> 15:20.496
I have no idea what women
are like nowadays.

15:20.564 --> 15:22.134
Last time I was on
the dating scene,

15:22.203 --> 15:23.640
Joe McCarthy was
on a rampage

15:23.707 --> 15:25.244
looking for anything red.

15:25.312 --> 15:27.150
Oh, back then I called
my penis Joe McCarthy.

15:27.219 --> 15:28.388
Look, relax, will ya?

15:28.455 --> 15:30.427
Here, I got these
off a Web site

15:30.495 --> 15:32.834
that tells you good things
to say when hot women walk by.

15:32.902 --> 15:34.339
Ooh, here comes a hot one.

15:34.407 --> 15:36.111
Say the first thing
on the list.

15:36.179 --> 15:38.519
Um, I-I love getting
trendy cupcakes

15:38.586 --> 15:40.391
in the middle of the
day for no reason.

15:40.459 --> 15:41.595
No way. So do I.

15:41.663 --> 15:42.799
Hi. I'm Paula.

15:42.866 --> 15:44.136
Carter. How do you do.

15:44.204 --> 15:45.574
Hey, why don't you
and your friend

15:45.642 --> 15:47.144
come join us over
at our table.

15:47.213 --> 15:48.550
Peter Griffin.
How do you do.

15:48.617 --> 15:50.489
(sputtering laugh)

15:50.557 --> 15:52.362
We would--
we would love to.

15:54.202 --> 15:56.709
Hey, girls, these are
my two new friends.

15:56.777 --> 15:58.413
Hello, ladies.
My name is Carter,

15:58.481 --> 16:00.754
and I require a tremendous
amount of calcium.

16:00.821 --> 16:01.958
Carter, come here.

16:02.025 --> 16:03.630
Sit next to me.

16:03.698 --> 16:04.832
Oh, this is--
this is fun.

16:04.901 --> 16:06.103
We're having fun.

16:06.172 --> 16:07.742
Hey, what do you say
we get some drinks.

16:07.810 --> 16:09.280
Hey, boy, boy,

16:09.349 --> 16:10.752
fetch me a John
Barrymore and soda

16:10.820 --> 16:12.222
and three Myrna Loys
for the women.

16:12.290 --> 16:13.260
(women gasp)

16:13.327 --> 16:14.497
Excuse me?

16:14.564 --> 16:16.670
What the hell is
your problem, you jerk?

16:16.738 --> 16:19.779
What? Does he belong
to somebody else?

16:19.847 --> 16:22.688
Come on, girls, let's ditch
this racist dick.

16:22.756 --> 16:24.461
What happened?
Did we get laid?

16:24.529 --> 16:26.567
You jackass. Those women
were coming on to you

16:26.634 --> 16:27.671
and you blew it.

16:27.738 --> 16:29.309
Now we got to go
to another club

16:29.376 --> 16:30.713
and start all over again.

16:30.781 --> 16:33.154
Peter, I don't want
to go to another club.

16:33.222 --> 16:35.394
I don't want women like that.

16:35.462 --> 16:38.035
I... I want Babs.

16:38.104 --> 16:39.440
Babs?

16:39.508 --> 16:41.112
You got a room full
of chicks like that

16:41.180 --> 16:42.416
and you're thinking
about Babs?

16:42.484 --> 16:44.121
She looks like someone
farted in a shoe.

16:44.189 --> 16:47.900
I had a moment of weakness, but
I-I know now that I was wrong.

16:47.967 --> 16:49.873
I need her, Peter.

16:49.941 --> 16:51.110
I love her.

16:51.177 --> 16:53.116
You-you got to help me
get her back.

16:53.183 --> 16:54.922
Well, it's probably
the right move anyway.

16:54.989 --> 16:56.660
Those girls seemed
kind of annoying.

16:56.727 --> 16:58.900
Look at them over there
taking a group picture together.

16:58.968 --> 17:00.405
I love you!

17:00.472 --> 17:01.575
I love you!

17:01.642 --> 17:03.213
We're all such good friend!

17:03.281 --> 17:05.888
You can tell by the way we're
pressing our faces together.

17:08.966 --> 17:11.639
And that's where
fat girls come from.

17:13.881 --> 17:15.919
All right, if I've learned
anything from romantic comedies

17:15.987 --> 17:18.694
it's that the ex-wife
always falls in love
with her husband again

17:18.762 --> 17:20.099
after he befriends
a little kid.

17:20.167 --> 17:21.236
Okay.

17:21.304 --> 17:23.376
And the kid needs
to be really cute.

17:23.443 --> 17:25.383
So I ordered
Jonathan Lipnicki.
(doorbell ringing)

17:25.450 --> 17:27.020
Ah, there's the cute
little guy now.

17:27.087 --> 17:28.625
Hang on.

17:28.693 --> 17:29.728
(door opening)

17:29.796 --> 17:31.902
Oh, my God!
What happened to you!

17:31.970 --> 17:34.476
Oh! Oh! We-we got to
get you to the hospital!

17:34.544 --> 17:36.049
Aah! Aah! You're hideous!

17:36.115 --> 17:37.318
Who did this to you?!

17:37.386 --> 17:38.823
Oh, oh, where are my keys?

17:38.892 --> 17:40.429
Where's my keys?!
Where are my keys?!

17:40.496 --> 17:41.833
Peter, what about Babs?

17:41.901 --> 17:43.906
Forget about yourself
for a second, Carter.

17:43.973 --> 17:46.280
Look what has happened
to Jonathan Lipnicki.

17:46.347 --> 17:47.650
Oh, yeah.

17:47.719 --> 17:48.955
No, you're,
you're, you're right.

17:49.023 --> 17:50.392
You should probably
take care of that.

17:50.460 --> 17:52.198
I'll-I'll-I'll
be-- I'll be here.

17:54.339 --> 17:55.575
All right, look, Carter,

17:55.643 --> 17:56.913
I think this will
definitely work.

17:56.981 --> 17:58.417
Now as soon as she sees you,

17:58.485 --> 18:00.021
you've got to do
exactly what I...

18:00.090 --> 18:01.995
Hey, whose Duesenberg is that
parked in the driveway?

18:04.002 --> 18:07.981
There's only one man I know
who drives a Duesenberg.

18:08.047 --> 18:14.534
♪ And I will buy you
laudanum and rhubarb cakes ♪

18:14.602 --> 18:21.121
♪ To balance out your
fragile body's humours. ♪

18:21.189 --> 18:23.762
Oh, Babs, I don't
wish to overwhelm you

18:23.830 --> 18:26.069
with my passions,
but I must say this.

18:26.137 --> 18:27.574
I'm ever so content.

18:27.641 --> 18:30.315
Oh, I am too, Rodginald.

18:30.382 --> 18:32.323
Do you think
perhaps one day,

18:32.390 --> 18:35.297
if we should marry, that
I could sit beside you?

18:35.365 --> 18:37.705
Yes, I think
that would be fine.

18:37.772 --> 18:40.379
Get away from my wife,
you rascal!

18:40.447 --> 18:43.356
Oh, such language
in the presence of a lady.

18:43.424 --> 18:46.432
If it's a row you want,
I will cleave you in twixt!

18:46.500 --> 18:49.207
Hang-hang on, Carter,
I think I know how to
take this guy down.

18:49.275 --> 18:50.344
Penis.

18:50.412 --> 18:52.149
(gasps)

18:52.217 --> 18:54.824
Carter, get out of here
this instant!

18:54.892 --> 18:56.931
I don't ever want
to see you again.

18:56.999 --> 18:59.004
Pussycup, please.

18:59.072 --> 19:01.779
Mrs. Pewterschmidt,
Carter has something
important to say to you.

19:01.846 --> 19:04.454
I'll set the mood.

19:04.522 --> 19:08.801
(singing romantically):
♪ B-B-Bird, bird, bird ♪

19:08.868 --> 19:10.740
♪ B-Bird's the word ♪

19:10.808 --> 19:14.151
♪ B-B-Bird, bird, bird ♪

19:14.219 --> 19:16.792
♪ B-Bird's the word ♪

19:16.860 --> 19:22.009
♪ Well, uh, don't you
know about the bird? ♪

19:22.076 --> 19:27.860
♪ Well, everybody knows
that the bird is the word. ♪

19:27.927 --> 19:30.535
Uh, Peter, I kind of want
to do this on my own.

19:30.603 --> 19:33.276
Babs, I need you.

19:33.344 --> 19:36.888
Cheating on you was the
worst mistake of my life.

19:36.955 --> 19:39.463
I kneel before you
a frightened soul

19:39.531 --> 19:40.766
and a broken man.

19:40.834 --> 19:43.007
A man who has nothing
without you.

19:43.075 --> 19:44.845
Give me one more chance,

19:44.913 --> 19:48.423
and I pledge to place above you
nothing-- not even myself--

19:48.491 --> 19:51.967
for all my time here,
and for time forever.

19:52.036 --> 19:54.843
Please, I beg you.

19:56.081 --> 19:59.892
Carter, what you did
was unforgivable.

19:59.960 --> 20:02.366
And as beautiful
as your words are,

20:02.434 --> 20:06.044
I... I just don't know
that they can fix what's done.

20:06.112 --> 20:08.752
I know I can't
do it overnight,

20:08.820 --> 20:11.094
but we can still have
a lot of years together.

20:11.162 --> 20:13.868
Please, just let me try.

20:13.936 --> 20:18.316
Carter, you had sex
with that woman.

20:18.384 --> 20:21.392
So, no, I can't trust you.

20:21.459 --> 20:25.337
But at my age, I'm certainly
not going to remarry either.

20:25.405 --> 20:28.681
So, if you'd like
to move back in

20:28.749 --> 20:32.292
and take things slowly
one step at a time,

20:32.360 --> 20:34.900
I suppose I can
give you the chance

20:34.968 --> 20:36.439
to earn my trust again.

20:36.506 --> 20:38.612
That sounds like a lot
of work. Go to hell!

20:38.679 --> 20:40.083
Carter, what-what-what-
what are we here for?

20:40.151 --> 20:41.186
What are we here for?

20:41.254 --> 20:42.423
All right, all right, fine.

20:42.491 --> 20:45.900
I'm... I'm...
I'm gonna try.

20:51.083 --> 20:52.755
Come here, you.

21:02.519 --> 21:05.161
Hey look, I found
a genie's lamp.

21:05.228 --> 21:06.932
<i>PETER:
Oh, no?</i>

21:07.000 --> 21:08.570
<i>Okay, maybe next week.</i>

21:08.571 --> 22:09.571
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru